From 3a2ef6303c716c68aa44bdebf94b650d295bf3bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:46:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 139/139] xdg: window geometry as the window; frame crops it;
 tiled states; decoration mode reloads

Clients with client-side shadows and resize margins (Chrome: geometry
16,10 on a buffer 32 x 42 px larger; GTK) were counted at their buffer
size: placement, maximize and zones used a box larger than the visible
window, and with the server's frame (EnforceServer: Chrome keeps its own
margins) the frame enclosed the transparent margins, leaving gaps and dark
strips between the frame and the window.

- The surface's size is the xdg window geometry; the window commits the
  geometry's size (the extents fallback keeps its offset correction).
- In the server's frame, the content is cropped to the window geometry.
- Snapped or tiled windows (zones) get the xdg tiled states, so GTK and
  Chrome drop their shadows and round corners there: The window fills the
  zone. Restoring clears them.
- 'Decoration' Mode is re-read on SIGHUP (new windows).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
